WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.860
Year after year, a ton of incredible films
are released only to end up going largely

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.979
unnoticed, and 2018 is no different.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.640
But don't worry about missing out on all the
future classics slipping under the radar:

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.540
we've got the scoop on the very best.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.760
Writer-director Chloé Zhao 's The Rider breaks
the barriers of what a true story film can

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.260
be.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.840
Real-life South Dakota rodeo rider Brady Jandreau
leads as a faintly fictionalized version of

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:29.009
himself, and recounts the horror of the moment
a horse trampled him, and the hardships he

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:30.280
faced afterwards.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:34.620
Though shaken and stripped of the very thing
that gave him purpose, Brady refuses to succumb

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.220
to sorrow and journeys across the badlands
to find a new identity.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.760
Jandreau's performance comes across nuanced
and naturalistic, gorgeously complemented

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.640
by shots of the South Dakota sky.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.820
On the whole, the film's ability to deliver
its dizzying narrative in a beautiful package

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.260
makes it critically acclaimed but unfortunately
underseen.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.720
In Academy Award-winning director Sebastián
Lelio's Disobedience, wanting what you can't

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.600
have isn't just a simple taboo.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.940
Disobedience stars Rachel Weisz as Ronit,
a non-practicing Orthodox Jewish woman who

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:09.550
returns to her buttoned-up London community
decades after her teenage romance with a female

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.940
school friend was found out.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.920
Rachel McAdams plays Esti, the childhood friend
who still holds the passion for Ronit in her

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.680
adulthood that she did in her youth.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.060
Once reunited, the two fall into their feelings
once more, a dynamic made more complicated

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.090
when Esti's husband Dovid gets involved.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:31.061
Balancing risky dramatic material with a poignant
rumination on centuries-long values, Lelio

00:01:31.061 --> 00:01:35.500
creates a film that swirls with strife as
intensely as it stupefies with its eventual

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.000
truths.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.940
"So everything was alright when I left?"

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:40.640
"No…

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.640
I was… ill."

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:49.200
Adapted from Jim Shepard's psychological fiction
novel Project X, And Then I Go chronicles

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.080
middle schooler Edwin's mounting stress as
it snowballs into insomnia and anxiety.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.140
Edwin's world changes after his best friend
Flake suffers a particularly humiliating encounter

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.900
with a bully and suggests that he and Edwin
silence their tormentors.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:08.300
What unravels after Flake's idea is an intimate
look into the peaks of violence and pain Edwin

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.670
rides through, and how the two boys' suppressed
fury fuels their terrifying, life-or-death

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.400
plan to finally be accepted.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.340
Ethan Hawke gives the performance of a lifetime
in First Reformed, the mesmerizing loss-of-faith

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.080
drama thriller from writer-director Paul Schrader.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.430
Hawke plays Reverend Ernst Toller, a middle-aged
pastor who works at a centuries-old Dutch

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.720
Reform church that draws in more tourists
than it does parishioners.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:36.380
Grappling with his own grief and dependence
issues, Toller faces a harrowing new challenge

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.160
when he meets pregnant parishioner Mary and
her suicidal husband Michael.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:45.480
Michael's radical beliefs compound Toller's
spiritual crisis, which leads to his final,

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.000
violent trial in an ending that will leave
you with plenty to think about.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.480
This isn't your mama's movie about parenthood.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:57.080
From director Jason Reitman and writer Diablo
Cody, Tully stars Charlize Theron as Marlo,

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.840
a struggling mother of two who's pregnant
with her third child.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.670
At Marlo's baby shower for her daughter, her
wealthy brother Craig offers to gift her a

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.820
night nanny, a young woman named Tully.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.700
Though reluctant at first, Marlo later agrees
to Craig's proposition, and she, her husband

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.400
Drew, and Tully embark on a mind-bending journey
that marries humor with surprising sincerity.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.500
Led by up-and-comer Elsie Fisher, Eighth Grade
follows 13-year-old Kayla Day as she completes

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.080
her final week of middle school.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:29.580
Kayla is awkward but well-meaning: she creates
motivational YouTube videos and encourages

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:33.540
others to carry themselves with confidence
that she doesn't seem to have herself.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:38.860
She's every young teenage girl, and Bo Burnham's
writing and direction perfectly captures that

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.640
in a sweet, heartwarming, true-to-life movie.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.580
"One more week of eighth grade, right?"

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:44.240
"Yeah."

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.000
"That's crazy."

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.400
"Yeah, huh."

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.700
"I can't believe you're gonna be in high school."

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.420
"Mm-hm."

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:55.480
From Academy Award-nominated director and
co-writer Debra Granik, Leave No Trace begins

00:03:55.489 --> 00:04:00.069
just before the boiling point: war veteran
Will and his 13-year-old daughter Tom have

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:02.700
been living in an isolated section of a public
park.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.720
When the survivalist duo make one small misstep,
social services come calling, taking them

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.480
in for extensive evaluations and setting them
up with everything they need to live a normal

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:11.980
life.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.780
Though confused as to why anyone would have
previously considered her and her father homeless,

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:20.820
Tom tries her hardest to adapt to her new
environment and embrace her surroundings;

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:25.200
her father, however, grows increasingly rigid
as both father and daughter try to understand

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.650
each other and their place in the world.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.660
"Think it might be easier on us if we try
to adapt."

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.140
"We're in their clothes, we're in their house,
we're..."

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:40.830
Fifteen years after the death of children's
television pioneer Fred Rogers, director Morgan

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.200
Neville invites audiences to celebrate the
life of the benevolent host of Mister Rogers'

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.260
Neighborhood and honor the good-heartedness
and empathy he taught.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:52.660
More than just a single-subject documentary,
Won't You Be My Neighbor?

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.500
examines Rogers for who he was outside the
PBS series and beneath his cozy cardigans.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:02.780
It reminds viewers that Rogers was far more
amazing than anyone knew, the kind of compassionate

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.140
creative that the world could use many more
of.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.040
Anyone who doubted Nick Offerman's ability
to play characters other than the mustachioed

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.280
Ron Swanson on Parks and Recreation needs
to watch Hearts Beat Loud.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:19.440
Offerman shines as Brooklyn-based widower
and musician Frank in the Brett Haley-directed

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:24.140
drama that brings together the magic of music
and the intricacies of a father-daughter relationship.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:28.630
When Frank and his daughter Sam find success
after Frank uploads one of their songs to

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.960
Spotify, their lives shift in a new direction.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.380
Rather than explore what happens to a parent
and a child who hit the road like real rock-and-rollers,

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.870
Hearts Beat Loud pulls the story inward, documenting
Frank's fears of his daughter leaving New

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:45.240
York, Sam's blossoming feelings for her girlfriend
Rose, and the pair's dual acceptance that

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.840
life may be scary, but that's what makes it
beautiful.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:53.080
Everyone who took a high school-level psychology
class will know that one of the most popular

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:58.050
debates in the field is that of nature versus
nurture, whether we are the way we are because

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:59.960
of our genetics or because of our upbringing.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:06.140
Three Identical Strangers, an equally harrowing
and heartwarming documentary by Tim Wardle,

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:11.251
sticks that question under a microscope as
it centers on Bobby, Eddy, and David, identical

00:06:11.251 --> 00:06:14.950
triplets who were separated at birth, each
adopted by different families of different

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.440
socioeconomic classes.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:22.590
The trio discover one another by chance in
1980, 19 years after their birth; Bobby and

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:27.080
Eddy found out they were "twins" after Bobby
was mistaken for Eddy on their college campus,

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.900
and David learned he was the third brother
following press coverage of Bobby and Eddy's

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:31.400
reunion.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:36.240
But the joy-filled homecomings quickly turn
dark as the triplets search for answers behind

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.720
their adoptions, which lead them to shocking,
life-altering secrets they were likely never

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:41.720
meant to uncover.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.570
Based on Emily M. Danforth's 2012 novel of
the same name, The Miseducation of Cameron

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:52.490
Post centers on Chloë Grace Moretz's Cameron
Post, who is outed as a lesbian when she's

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.240
caught kissing her female best friend.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:59.500
Soon after, Cameron's conservative aunt orders
her to undergo conversion therapy at a center

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.080
called God's Promise.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:05.380
There, Cameron forms friendships with a handful
of other teens who, like her, put up a fight

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.980
against being "re-educated."

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.560
It's a stirring coming-of-age movie that's
absolutely worth seeing.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:16.540
Rafael Casal and Daveed Diggs prove to be
triple-threat talents in Blindspotting, the

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.660
comedy-drama the pair wrote, produced, and
starred in under the direction of first-time

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.180
feature filmmaker Carlos López Estrada.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:28.380
Diggs leads as Collin, a felon who's so close
to the end of his year-long probation, he

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.660
can practically taste it.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:34.900
Casal plays his best friend Miles, a troublemaker
who offers no support to Collin in helping

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.560
him make it through the fateful final 72 hours
of his sentencing.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:44.150
Where Collin longs for a new beginning, Miles
actively seeks out danger in the rapidly gentrifying

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.940
streets of Oakland, California.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:51.180
The pair's lives splinter when Collin witnesses
a white cop kill a black man, and Miles' fixation

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:55.920
on violence and his increasingly trigger-happy
mentality threatens to have devastating consequences.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:00.280
Those who missed out on seeing Blindspotting
in its original release should remedy that

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:05.750
misstep ASAP, and see why critics are calling
this provocative, timely, wholly underappreciated

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.040
movie one of the most unique films of 2018.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.900
"You went to jail on a fire technicality."

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:11.580
"Did I?"

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:12.460
"Yes!

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.200
How were we supposed to know hipsters are
so flammable?"

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:22.180
Regina Hall leads Support the Girls as Lisa,
the general manager of Double Whammies, a

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.180
Hooters-esque restaurant.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:27.520
Lisa and her co-workers are trying to make
it as well as they can in the world of customer

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.900
service, until they find themselves stuck
in a particularly heinous day.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:35.060
Lisa tries to hold it together, but every
hour seems to bring even more problems.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:38.520
The real world bites, the girls learn, but
they bite back.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:43.880
Support the Girls is rock-solid and rollicking,
able to handle heavy themes while still remaining

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:44.440
buoyant.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:50.000
Writer-director Crystal Moselle takes viewers
to the concrete jungle, to the inner workings

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:54.350
of a young woman's mind, and to the half-pipes,
tramps, and grinding rails of New York's many

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:57.220
skateparks in the down-to-earth drama Skate
Kitchen.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.850
The film is an R-rated exercise in just how
good movies can be when they're simplistic

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:02.780
and realistic.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.620
The movie follows introverted teenager Camille
who joins the all-girl skateboarding group

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:08.260
Skate Kitchen.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.980
Camille's world cracks open wide thereafter:
she leaves home, begins falling for her new

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.600
roommate's ex-boyfriend, fosters confidence,
and fights misogyny.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.240
Most importantly, she learns how great life
can be with a pack of like-minded ladies at

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:21.960
your side.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:27.720
In the mystery-thriller Searching, John Cho
stars as David Kim, the father of 16-year-old

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.560
Margot, who goes missing without a trace after
visiting a friend's house for a group study

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.060
session.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:37.120
David begins searching for answers in Margot's
laptop, retracing the steps she took online

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.420
in hopes of bringing her home before it's
too late.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:44.320
What follows is a heart-stopping, jaw-dropping
journey to uncover the truth behind his daughter's

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.400
disappearance, which is darker and more complex
than David could have ever imagined.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:53.370
With its unique approach, well-sustained suspense,
tight pacing, and a final twist you'll never

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:58.300
see coming, Searching is one of the best movies
of 2018, and the most original thrillers in

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.300
recent memory.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:04.800
Joaquin Phoenix and John C. Reilly star as
sibling gunslingers Charlie and Eli Sisters

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:09.920
in director Jacques Audiard's witty and emotionally
weighty Western The Sisters Brothers.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:15.660
Adapted from Patrick deWitt's novel of the
same name, the 1851-set film follows the rebellious,

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.520
liquor-loving Charlie and the contemplative
Eli as they travel through the northwest United

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:22.080
States on the hunt for chemist Hermann Warm.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.240
Hermann has created a formula for prospecting
gold, which makes him a target for the Sisters'

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.780
boss and a detective played by Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:33.380
Unpredictable and atmospheric, with a story
made all the more enjoyable by Phoenix and

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:37.460
Reilly's brilliant performances, The Sisters
Brothers is a Western that you should see

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:38.710
as soon as possible.

